       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is typically given as 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI suspect one of these was intended:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg per dose**, which are more common starting or maintenance doses.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily really is what you intend, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
